🚀 Automated CI/CD Pipeline on AWS
Project Overview
This project demonstrates a fully automated CI/CD (Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment) pipeline built on AWS cloud infrastructure. Every time code is pushed to GitHub, Jenkins automatically builds, tests, and deploys the application to AWS EC2 — with zero manual intervention!

🎯 Problem This Project Solves

**Before CI/CD (Manual Way):**
* Developer writes code
* Someone manually downloads it
* Someone manually builds it
* Someone manually tests it
* Someone manually deploys it
* Takes hours or days
* Human errors happen frequently
* Inconsistent deployments

**After CI/CD (This Project):**
* Developer writes code
* Types: git push
* Everything else happens automatically
* Deployed within a minute
* Zero human errors
* Consistent every time

Architecture
Developer Laptop
       |
       | git push
       |
GitHub Repository
       |
       | Webhook triggers automatically
       |
Jenkins on AWS EC2
       |
       |-- Stage 1: Pull code from GitHub
       |-- Stage 2: Install dependencies
       |-- Stage 3: Run automated tests
       |-- Stage 4: Build Docker image
       |-- Stage 5: Deploy container
       |-- Stage 6: Verify deployment
       |
       |
Application Live on EC2 (Port 3000)
       |
       |
CloudWatch Monitoring
       |
       |
SNS Email Alerts


