## 📋 Pipeline Stages

### Stage 1: Checkout
```
Pulls latest code from GitHub repository
automatically when webhook triggers
```
### Stage 2: Install Dependencies
```
Runs npm install to download all
Node.js libraries the app needs
```
### Stage 3: Run Tests
```
Runs npm test to verify code works
If tests fail → pipeline stops here
Broken code never reaches production!
```
### Stage 4: Build Docker Image
```
Runs docker build to package the app
with all its dependencies into a
portable container image
```
### Stage 5: Deploy Container
```
Stops old container
Starts new container with latest code
App immediately updated for users
```
### Stage 6: Verify Deployment
```
Confirms container is running
Verifies deployment was successful
Pipeline marked as SUCCESS ✅
```

## 🔧 Infrastructure Setup

**VPC Configuration:**
```
VPC CIDR: 10.0.0.0/16
Subnet: 10.0.1.0/24 (Public)
Internet Gateway: Attached
Route Table: 0.0.0.0/0 → IGW
```

**Security Group Rules:**
```
Port 22   → SSH (My IP only)
Port 8080 → Jenkins UI (Public)
Port 3000 → Web App (Public)
```

**EC2 Configuration:**
```
Instance Type: t3.small
AMI: Amazon Linux 2023
Storage: 20GB gp2
Java: Amazon Corretto 21
```

**IAM Role Permissions:**
```
AmazonS3FullAccess
CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy
AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryFullAccess
```

